"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,625\nThe Learning Brain. Series 4: Habits\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,416\nEpisode 11\n\n3\n00:00:07,496 --> 00:00:10,408\nMindset, with realistic effects\n\n4\n00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:17,627\nGrowth mindset is the belief that your abilities can develop through effort,\n\n5\n00:00:17,957 --> 00:00:20,243\ngood strategies, and help from others.\n\n6\n00:00:20,609 --> 00:00:22,888\nIt is on posters in many schools.\n\n7\n00:00:23,209 --> 00:00:26,009\nBut how much does it actually change results?\n\n8\n00:00:26,179 --> 00:00:29,329\nThe biggest test was published in 2019.\n\n9\n00:00:29,862 --> 00:00:37,687\nMore than twelve thousand ninth graders across the United States did either a growth mindset program or a control activity: two short online sessions,\n\n10\n00:00:38,210 --> 00:00:41,966\nunder an hour in total.\n\n11\n00:00:42,261 --> 00:00:44,104\nAmong lower achieving students,\n\n12\n00:00:44,363 --> 00:00:47,141\ngrades rose by about a tenth of a grade point,\n\n13\n00:00:47,591 --> 00:00:52,668\nand the share with a D or F average fell by more than five percentage points.\n\n14\n00:00:53,187 --> 00:00:59,272\nBoth higher and lower achievers were also a little more likely to take advanced math the next year.\n\n15\n00:00:59,442 --> 00:01:04,332\nThe effect was larger in schools where classmates valued taking on hard work.\n\n16\n00:01:04,942 --> 00:01:08,640\nThe researchers compared it to a seed that needs fertile soil.\n\n17\n00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:11,533\nMeta-analyses tell a more modest story.\n\n18\n00:01:11,943 --> 00:01:17,156\nIn 2018, the average effect of mindset programs on achievement was tiny,\n\n19\n00:01:17,425 --> 00:01:18,976\nabout point zero eight.\n\n20\n00:01:19,519 --> 00:01:24,976\nA 2023 review found that the highest quality studies showed little or no benefit,\n\n21\n00:01:25,312 --> 00:01:30,297\nand that authors with a financial stake were more likely to report positive results.\n\n22\n00:01:30,718 --> 00:01:34,520\nAnother found meaningful effects for students at academic risk.\n\n23\n00:01:34,981 --> 00:01:36,515\nThe debate continues.\n\n24\n00:01:36,685 --> 00:01:37,908\nSo, some caution.\n\n25\n00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:40,115\nEffects are small on average,\n\n26\n00:01:40,135 --> 00:01:41,698\nand depend on context.\n\n27\n00:01:42,081 --> 00:01:44,061\nA mindset is one ingredient,\n\n28\n00:01:44,081 --> 00:01:45,066\nnot a fix.\n\n29\n00:01:45,352 --> 00:01:48,294\nAnd growth comes from effort plus better strategies,\n\n30\n00:01:48,408 --> 00:01:49,640\nnot effort alone.\n\n31\n00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:50,669\nTry this.\n\n32\n00:01:50,975 --> 00:01:52,220\nWhen you get a bad mark,\n\n33\n00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,368\nask what it tells you,\n\n34\n00:01:53,388 --> 00:01:54,826\nand what you will change.\n\n35\n00:01:55,212 --> 00:01:57,004\nPair effort with a new strategy,\n\n36\n00:01:57,024 --> 00:01:59,348\nlike self testing instead of rereading.\n\n37\n00:01:59,732 --> 00:02:01,072\nAsk for help early.\n\n38\n00:02:01,356 --> 00:02:02,258\nAnd now and then,\n\n39\n00:02:02,278 --> 00:02:04,224\nchoose a challenge you might fail.\n\n40\n00:02:04,394 --> 00:02:05,736\nAbilities can grow.\n\n41\n00:02:05,902 --> 00:02:07,582\nStrategies make it happen.\n\n"
